  "methodology": "Four denoiser models/functions, one preparation and release per fresh native process, without inference. Pair order alternates serial/batch then batch/serial. Same pinned build for both arms. Full source hashes are streamed before every arm; SDK/OS caches are retained, without a cache purge.",
  "timing_scope": "Primary preparation timing starts after Runtime initialization and ends when all four segment functions are ready. Separate complete timing includes release/flush. Native model and function invocation events measure both batch phases. Whole checker timing also includes source verification and Swift schedule preparation.",
  "rss_scope": "Every arm runs a fresh Python checker, so its cumulative RUSAGE_CHILDREN peak is separate from other arms. Each peak still includes that checker's preparation helpers. Retain before/after counters; do not subtract high-water marks or add RSS to Metal accounting.",
  "launcher_scope": "When launched via REA at the Python entry point, native Rust children have no requested breakpoints. Launch/observation overhead remains outside the driver phase timers.",
